  "definition": "Vitalism is the view that life depends on a special vital principle separate from physical and chemical forces, so physics and chemistry alone cannot fully explain living processes. It contrasts with mechanistic materialism and was also used to explain why organic and inorganic materials were thought to behave differently when heated.",
